<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04XN">Remark <span data-tag="04XN">10.2.3.19</span> <span class="named">(Functoriality of Images)</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $\operatorname{Fun}'( \Delta ^2, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \subseteq \operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^2, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ be the full subcategory described in Proposition <a data-tag="04XH" href="/tag/04XH">10.2.3.14</a>. Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ has images if and only if the restriction functor </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  D: \operatorname{Fun}'( \Delta ^2, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^1, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \quad \quad \sigma \mapsto d^{2}_{1}( \sigma ) \]
</div>
<p> is a trivial Kan fibration. If this condition is satisfied, then $D$ admits a section which carries each morphism $f: X \rightarrow Y$ of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ to a $2$-simplex </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  \operatorname{im}(f) \ar [dr] &amp;  \\ X \ar [ur] \ar [rr]^{f} &amp;  &amp;  Y } \]
</div>
<p> which exhibits $\operatorname{im}(f)$ as an image of $f$. In particular, we can promote the construction $f \mapsto \operatorname{im}(f)$ as a functor of $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{Fun}(\Delta ^1,\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. </p>
</article>
